       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. The 1,700 mg single dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 to 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max labeled dose)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- Another dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm it. I can then enter it with a note that you verified the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
